This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

This is a long-running multi-round iterative fix project on a single production file, `tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/index.html` (an "Alunix" digital agency one-page site with scroll-choreographed sections). The conversation covers rounds R5 through R8 (all completed, each ending with "V3d RN klar"), and R9 (just started, not yet worked on beyond initial reads).

**R9 (the current, active round)** — the user's exact message:

> "Alunix, V3d runda 9: tre mobilfynd från Astra. Cell V3d, ut-mapp `tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d`, port 3304.
>
> Läs `tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/reviews/r8-astra.md`. Svaret är `fix`, med tre material_fixes, och alla gäller bara 390. Vid 1440 håller varje PARITET-rad. **Ingenting vid 1440 får ändras.** Bevisen ligger i `tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/shots/astra-r8/`.
>
> 1. **Hōrais citat syns inte vid 390.** Vid `case-horai-03` ligger citatet bakom sajtens egen nav, eftersom ramens innerhöjd är 450 px. Orsaken är Hōrais egen layout, och `sites/*` rörs aldrig. Lös det med ramens höjd eller med ankaret på vår sida.
>    **Mål:** citatet syns helt i ramen, under navens underkant.
> 2. **Tomt blått band i tesbandet vid 390.** Det är 285 px mellan tickstrecken och fotot, och fotot är 343×215. Orsaken är att figuren ärver `align-self:end` och fotolådan har `aspect-ratio:16/10`.
>    **Mål:** högst 32 px mellan strecken och fotot, och fotot minst 400 px högt, eller en komposition som fyller skärmen utan ett tomt band.
> 3. **Calyx steg 03 vid 390.** Ramen visar ett foto, men dess bildtext ligger nedanför ramen.
>    **Mål:** minst ett foto med sin bildtext helt inne i ramen.
>
> ## Gör
> - Kör `Skill(design)` först.
> - Skriv planen `tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/plans/056-astra-r8-mobil.md`.
> - Använd kirurgiska `Edit`. Copyn rörs inte.
>
> ## Verifiera
> - Ta enskilda skärmbilder (inga kontaktark som bevis) vid 390 och 375 för `?preview=thesis-01..05`, `case-horai-03` och `case-calyx-03`, och i hjulsekvens genom samma lägen. Läs dem.
> - Ta samma lägen vid 1440 och jämför dem pixel för pixel mot före-bilderna i `astra-r8/ours/`. De ska vara oförändrade.
> - Kör en kort grind: noll horisontell scroll 320–1920, `a11y_scan` vid 390, låst copy 15/15 och noll tankstreck.
>
> Leverans: `NOTES.md` § V3d R9. Sista raden ska vara `V3d R9 klar` eller `[PAUSED — steg X]`."

Key constraints stated explicitly for R9:
- Only 390px width fixes; **nothing at 1440 may change** (strict, emphasized in bold by the user)
- `sites/*` (Calyx/Hōrai's own HTML) must never be touched — fixes for Hōrai's quote visibility must happen on our page's side (frame height or anchor), never in `sites/horai.html`
- Copy/text strings must not be touched
- Evidence for verification must be **individual screenshots, not contact sheets**
- 1440 screenshots must be pixel-compared against existing "before" images in `tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/shots/astra-r8/ours/`
- Surgical `Edit` only, plan file required before editing
- Short gate this round: 0 horizontal scroll 320-1920, `a11y_scan` at 390 only, locked copy 15/15, zero em-dashes (narrower than prior rounds' full gates)

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Scroll-choreography engine publishing `--sc-ps` per `data-sc-act` element; F-014: all bespoke motion reads `--sc-ps`-derived values, never raw `--sc-p`; F-011: motion always plays, `prefers-reduced-motion` must never be read anywhere (standing, project-wide).
   - Pinned "stage" mechanic (`data-sc-act="pin"` + `data-sc-stage` child) — the scroll engine (`scroll/scrollcraft.js`, `scroll/sc-smooth.js`) handles the pin/stage positioning itself; page-authored CSS on `.thesis-stage`/`.case-stage` is purely visual (background, grid layout), not the positioning mechanism.
   - CSS `clip-path: inset()` box-shorthand serialization: computed-style values collapse to 1–4 tokens depending on symmetry (e.g., `inset(0% 0px)` when top=bottom and left=right, `inset(100% 0px 0%)` when only left=right) — a naive fixed-token-count parser silently fails; must parse per CSS box-shorthand rules (1 value=all four; 2=top/bottom,left/right; 3=top,left/right,bottom; 4=top,right,bottom,left).
   - CSS custom property circular/self-reference: `.selector{--x:var(--x)}` on the same selector is invalid at computed-value time (not simply "inherits from outside") — the property becomes empty/invalid for that element, cascading failure into any `var(--x)` consumer (e.g., `background:var(--bg))` falling to `transparent`).
   - Asymmetric `--in`/`--out` clip-path timing windows for exclusive-visibility scroll-reveal: for element i with slice `[a,b]=[i/n,(i+1)/n]`, `--in` must open over `[a, a+f]` (from its own start) and `--out` must close over `[b-f, b]` (to its own end) — NOT symmetric `±f/2` windows around the same shared boundary point `b`, which causes simultaneous partial visibility of adjacent elements (the R8 bug, up to 130px overlap).
   - `data-sc-span` attribute setting a pin act's total scroll-track height in viewport-heights.
   - Same-origin iframe `contentWindow`/`contentDocument` access for embedded site sync: `measureCase()` reads target elements' `offsetTop`/`offsetHeight` directly inside the iframe's own document to compute scrollY targets, then `latchTick()` (in the main page's render loop) calls `contentWindow.scrollTo({top, left:0, behavior:'instant'})` driven by the parent act's lerped `--sc-ps` (via `cur`), never transforming the iframe element itself (a `PRODUCT.md` requirement: a shown live frame is never transformed/faded).
   - Tailwind CSS responsive height resolution inside embedded sites: a class stack like `h-[130vh] min-h-[1000px]` resolves differently depending on the iframe's actual rendered height (`ih`) — at large `ih`, `1.3*ih` dominates; at small `ih` (mobile), the `1000px` floor dominates — meaning a fixed ratio-based "centering" anchor computed for one `ih` regime breaks at another. Fix: compute anchors dynamically from the target element's *actual* `offsetHeight` at measurement time (`'center'` mode) rather than a hardcoded ratio.
   - `sites/horai.html:157-173`: `.quote-section` is `overflow-hidden` at `h-[130vh] min-h-[1000px]` with an inner `sticky` column at `487px`; a CSS `sticky` element never engages ("sticks") within an `overflow: hidden` ancestor unless that ancestor is scrollable — meaning at a short enough embedding frame, the sticky-driven quote can never be both "formed" (section scrolled to center) and visible simultaneously; this is an intrinsic property of the embedded site, explicitly out of scope to fix (`sites/*` never touched).
   - CSS Grid `align-self`/`grid-row` cascade: a mobile `@media` override that redefines `grid-column`/`grid-row`/`display`/`flex-direction` on an element does NOT reset properties like `align-self` or `aspect-ratio` set by an earlier (desktop-scoped) rule on the same selector — those keep cascading through unless explicitly overridden in the mobile block too. This was diagnosed by Astra as the root cause of R8's "fix 7" not actually working: `.thesis-figure`'s base rule sets `align-self:end`, never overridden at mobile, so the figure sits at the bottom of its grid row instead of stretching; `.thesis-photo-box`'s base rule sets `aspect-ratio:16/10`, never overridden at mobile, so even with `flex:1` added, the aspect-ratio locks height and prevents growth.
   - `contrast_over_media.py`'s known `background-clip:text` false-positive pattern (documented across many rounds, not directly relevant to R9 but part of established project lore).
   - CARL verification principle, explicitly demonstrated in R8: before trusting a "clean" (0 overlap) measurement result, re-run the same measurement tool against a **known-broken** case (the old symmetric `--in`/`--out` formula, reinjected via Playwright `add_style_tag` with `!important`) to confirm the tool actually detects the defect — this caught a real bug in my own measurement script (the clip-path token-count parser) that was silently reporting 0 overlap for both the broken AND fixed formulas until corrected.
   - `python -m http.server` is HTTP/1.0 and unreliable for this large file on Windows/Chromium — must use `skills/design/scripts/serve.py` (HTTP/1.1) on port 8795 for all local Playwright testing in this session.
   - Playwright `mouse.wheel` mandated for scroll-sequence captures (never `scrollTo` for "hjulsekvens" evidence, though direct `scrollTo` is acceptable for fast/targeted measurement scripts that aren't claiming to be "hjul" evidence).
   - `?preview=<mode>` URL parameter mechanism: sets `window.__scFreezeMotion=true` and forces the page to scroll/settle to a specific named state (e.g., `thesis-01`..`thesis-05`, `case-calyx-01`..`-05`, `case-horai-01`..`-06`, `curtain`, `chapter`, `cases`, `bridge`, `front`/`mid`/`back`, `process-01`..`-07`) via a shared `aimPin(el, p)` helper (for pin acts) or direct `window.scrollTo` (for the ridå/`ridaY()` mechanism, since the process-chapter's sticky-lift isn't a `--sc-ps`-driven act).

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/index.html`** — the single production file, all edits applied via surgical `Edit` calls across R5–R8. Below is the relevant CURRENT (end-of-R8) state that R9 must work against (exact line numbers will have shifted slightly and must be re-verified with fresh Grep/Read calls before editing in R9):

     **Tesbandet mobile CSS** (in `@media (max-width:767px)` under the `.thesis-stage` block, R8-era):
     ```css
     @media (max-width:767px){
       .thesis-stage{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-rows:auto auto 1fr;
         padding:clamp(56px,9svh,80px) var(--rail-x) clamp(20px,3svh,32px);row-gap:16px;}
       .thesis-lines{align-self:start;min-height:calc(4 * .98 * clamp(2rem,5vw + 1rem,6rem));}
       .thesis-figure{grid-column:1;grid-row:3;min-height:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;}
       .thesis-photo-box{border-right:1px solid var(--frame-line);flex:1;min-height:0;}
       .thesis-caption{padding-right:0;}
     }
     ```
     Base (desktop-scoped, but NOT overridden at mobile for these two specific properties) rules:
     ```css
     .thesis-figure{grid-column:2;grid-row:1 / span 2;align-self:end;min-width:0;margin:0;}
     .thesis-photo-box{position:relative;aspect-ratio:16/10;overflow:clip;
       border:1px solid var(--frame-line);border-right:0;}
     ```
     Per r8-astra.md's diagnosis, `align-self:end` (base) and `aspect-ratio:16/10` (base) both still apply inside the mobile media query since neither is explicitly reset there — this is why R8's fix 7 (adding `flex:1;min-height:0` to `.thesis-photo-box` and `1fr` to the grid row) did NOT actually work: the box never grows because aspect-ratio still governs its height, and the figure never stretches to fill the row because align-self:end pins it to the bottom. R9 fix 2 needs to add `align-self:stretch` to `.thesis-figure` and `aspect-ratio:auto` (or remove it) from `.thesis-photo-box`, both scoped inside the `@media (max-width:767px)` block.

     **Case mobile CSS** (in `@media (max-width:767px)` under `.case-stage`, governs both Calyx and Hōrai):
     ```css
     @media (max-width:767px){
       .case-stage,.case--horai .case-stage{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);
         grid-template-rows:58svh minmax(0,1fr);padding:0 0 clamp(16px,3svh,24px);}
       .case .case-fig{grid-column:1;grid-row:1;}
       .case .case-text{grid-column:1;grid-row:2;justify-content:flex-start;
         padding:clamp(16px,3svh,24px) var(--rail-x) 0;}
       .case-wrap,.case--calyx .case-wrap,.case--horai .case-wrap{border:0;
         border-bottom:1px solid var(--c-line-on-paper);}
       .case-text > .kicker-sans{display:none;}
       .case-title{font-size:clamp(2rem,9vw,2.5rem);margin-top:0;}
       .case-steps{margin-top:14px;}
       .cs h3{font-size:1.375rem;} .cs p{font-size:1rem;max-width:none;}
       .case-rail{display:none;}
     }
     ```
     `58svh` at 390×844 ≈ 489.5px for case-fig's row, minus the frame-cap caption's own height (~39px) ≈ 450px actual iframe height — matches Astra's measured "ramens innerhöjd är 450 px" / "451 px" exactly. r8-astra.md's material_fixes #1 explicitly cites `index.html:881` (this mobile row rule area) as one of two relevant edit points for the Hōrai quote fix (the other being the CASES anchor array).

     **CASES array + measureCase (JS, bottom `<script>` block)** — current state (R8-era):
     ```js
     var CASES = [
         { el: document.getElementById('case-calyx'), anchors: [
             ['top', 0], ['#studio', 0], ['#studio + section', 0], ['#index', 0], ['#commission', 0] ] },
         { el: document.getElementById('case-horai'), anchors: [
             ['top', 0], ['#hero-section + section', 0.30], ['#quote-section', 'center'],
             ['#quote-section + section', 0], ['#reservations', -1], ['#reservations', 0] ] }
       ].filter(function(C){ return C.el; });
       CASES.forEach(function(C){ C.last = -1; });
       function measureCase(C){
         var f = C.el.querySelector('iframe'), w = f && f.contentWindow, d = f && f.contentDocument;
         if (!d || !d.documentElement) return;
         var ih = w.innerHeight, max = d.documentElement.scrollHeight - ih;
         C.f = f; C.w = w; C.y = C.anchors.map(function(a){
           var el = a[0] === 'top' ? null : d.querySelector(a[0]);
           var t = el ? el.offsetTop : 0;
           var off = a[1] === 'center' ? (el ? (el.offsetHeight - ih) / 2 : 0) : a[1] * ih;
           return Math.max(0, Math.min(max, Math.round(t + off)));
         });
       }
     ```
     - Calyx's anchor index 2 (`['#studio + section', 0]`) corresponds to `case-calyx-03` (step 3, "Bilderna i par" per COPY-V3d-final.md) — this is the anchor r8-astra.md's material_fixes #3 says needs a new offset/figcaption-based anchor so the photo AND its caption both land inside the 450px mobile frame (currently anchored at the section's raw top, which shows the photo but pushes its caption to y=500, past the 450px frame boundary).
     - Hōrai's anchor index 2 (`['#quote-section', 'center']`) corresponds to `case-horai-03` — this is the R8 fix that works at 1440/768 but NOT at 390 per r8-astra.md's fidelity section ("Fix 4, Hōrais citat: öppen vid 390"), because true centering of a `min-h-[1000px]`-floored section inside a 450px frame necessarily pushes the quote content above/behind the frame's own nav (which occupies y=0..117 inside the embedded site). r8-astra.md's material_fixes #1 gives exact target numbers: `#quote-text`-top = ih − 507.5 when centered; offsetting the anchor `s` px above center gives opacity/blur 0.97/0.4px at s=100, 0.81/2.3px at s=200, 0.64/4.3px at s=272; concrete requirement: **ih ≥ 625 if anchor stays centered, OR ih ≥ 525 if anchor is set 100px above center** — implying the mobile case row height (`58svh` → something taller) is the more likely lever, since increasing the case-fig row height increases `ih` directly, whereas adjusting the anchor alone (without enough ih) still can't clear the nav overlap per the site's own overflow-hidden/sticky mechanics.

     **`.thesis-lines` min-height (mobile)** — already correctly reduced in R8 from `7 * .98 * fontsize` to `4 * .98 * fontsize` (139.16px, matching the longest sentence's actual 4-row wrap) — this part is NOT broken; the NEW 285px gap Astra found in R9's review is a DIFFERENT gap (between the ticks and the image), not the old gap (between the sentence and the ticks, which R8 fixed to 41px, confirmed fine).

   - **`tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/plans/056-astra-r8-mobil.md`** — NOT YET CREATED. Explicitly required by R9's instructions before any Edit calls.

   - **`tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/NOTES.md`** — contains `§ V3d R1` through `§ V3d R8` (all completed, each ending with `**V3d RN klar**`). R9's section (`§ V3d R9`) has NOT yet been started.

   - **`tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/reviews/r8-astra.md`** — READ IN FULL this round (contents captured in full in the tool-result above; key excerpts already quoted in section 2 and above). This is Astra's fourth review pass, confirming all of R8's material_fixes are closed EXCEPT three specific 390-width issues, which is exactly what R9 must resolve. Full content includes:
     - `## persistence`: methodology notes, confirms sweep tooling now uses a corrected computed-clip-path parser.
     - `## fidelity`: r7-fixes status recap (all 8 marked "stängd" except fix 4/Hōrai-citat and fix 7/tomt-band-vid-390, both marked "öppen"), plus full PARITET row-by-row (P01–P20, all "håller nivån" except P03/P17/P19 which "håller inte, vid 390" specifically — 1440 confirmed holding for all rows).
     - `## ceiling`: explains Hōrai's own quote-section CSS mechanics (`overflow-hidden` + `sticky`, why it can't work at short frame heights) — the key technical justification for why the fix must live on our page's side.
     - `## material_fixes`: the three fixes with exact target numbers, quoted fully in section 1 above and cross-referenced against code locations `index.html:2178`/`881` (Hōrai), `index.html:628`/`629`/`649`/`654` (tesbandet — note: R9's own user-relayed summary paraphrases this as "figuren ärver align-self:end... fotolådan aspect-ratio:16/10", matching my analysis above), `index.html:2176` (Calyx anchor).
     - `## keep`: reconfirms everything from R8 that must NOT regress (asymmetric --in/--out windows, Calyx paper background, case ramen sizing, Hyperborea 37.1%, ridaY(120), case sync monotonicity) — directly relevant since R9 must not touch any of this.

   - **`tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/shots/astra-r8/ours/`** — referenced by the user as the "before" baseline directory for the required 1440 pixel-for-pixel comparison. NOT YET READ/listed this round — I will need to enumerate its contents to know exactly which reference images exist for the pixel-diff step.

   - **`tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3d/COPY-V3d-final.md`** — the locked copy reference (established in R7), NOT re-read this round yet but relevant since R9 must not touch any copy strings; the 15 locked lines verified in R8 (via direct substring search) remain the standard to re-check in R9's gate.

4. Errors and fixes (all from R8, fully resolved, retained here for context since the same tooling/methodology will be reused in R9):
   - **Clip-path overlap measurement script gave false "0 overlap" for both broken and fixed CSS.** Root cause: `getComputedStyle(el).clipPath` serializes using CSS box-shorthand collapsing (1–4 tokens depending on symmetry, e.g. `inset(0% 0px)` when top=bottom and left=right), but my first parser assumed exactly 3 tokens (regex matching only `%`-suffixed values), silently failing (`len(m) != 4`) and skipping every element — meaning the "0 overlap" result was vacuous (nothing was ever actually measured), not evidence of correctness. Fixed by writing a proper box-shorthand-aware parser (1/2/3/4-token cases). **Validated per CARL principle**: re-ran the corrected parser against the OLD (known-broken) symmetric `--in`/--out` CSS (reinjected via `page.add_style_tag` with `!important`) and confirmed it now correctly reports 382.8px of overlap — only then trusted the "0px overlap" result for the actual (fixed) R8 code.
   - **Fix 4 (Hōrai quote) fixed ratio `+0.15` only worked at 1440, not 390.** Diagnosed via direct measurement: at 1440 (ih≈807), Hōrai's `h-[130vh]` Tailwind class dominates over its `min-h-[1000px]` floor (1.3×807=1049>1000), so the fixed ratio (derived assuming `H=1.3×ih` always) computed correctly (`0.15` = `(1.3ih)/(2ih)-0.5`, a width-independent ratio). At 390 (ih≈450), `1.3×450=585<1000`, so the `min-h-[1000px]` floor dominates instead, making the true section height 1000px (not `1.3×ih`) — the fixed 0.15 ratio was wrong for this regime (measured: jpOpacity 0.813, txtFilter blur(2.5px) instead of 1/0px). **Fixed** by replacing the fixed-ratio anchor with a dynamic `'center'` mode in `measureCase()` that reads the target element's actual `offsetHeight` at measurement time and computes true centering (`(offsetHeight - ih) / 2`), which self-corrects regardless of which Tailwind class wins at a given `ih`. Re-verified: opacity=1, blur=0px at ALL THREE widths (1440, 768, 390) after this JS change — however, r8-astra.md (read at the start of R9) reveals this JS-level centering fix is STILL insufficient at 390 specifically, because even a perfectly centered `min-h-[1000px]` section, when the frame itself is only 450px tall, necessarily positions the quote content behind/above the site's own nav bar (nav occupies iframe y=0..117) — this is the NEW problem R9 must solve, requiring either a taller mobile frame (`ih`) or an anchor offset large enough to clear the nav, per r8-astra.md's explicit numeric targets (ih≥625 if centered, or ih≥525 with a 100px-above-center offset).

5. Problem Solving:
   - R5 through R8 fully resolved all reported material_fixes through each round, with extensive verification each time (motion_probe with staircase/reversals/max_step checks validated at cpu 1 fine-wheel settings, positioned via `?preview=` since organic top-of-page scroll didn't reach deep acts within reasonable tick budgets; contrast_over_media checks; a11y_scan/reflow/tab_walk; word-break scripts; locked-copy substring checks; inline-hex count-vs-baseline checks; horizontal overflow sweeps at 8 widths).
   - **R8's own fixes for the tesbandet mobile empty-band (fix 7) and Hōrai's mobile quote visibility (fix 4) turned out to be INCOMPLETE**, discovered by Astra's NEXT review (r8-astra.md, read at the start of R9): fix 7 moved the empty gap rather than eliminating it (old 243px gap between sentence-and-ticks became a NEW 285px gap between ticks-and-image, because the underlying CSS cascade issue — base-rule `align-self:end`/`aspect-ratio:16/10` not reset at mobile — was never actually addressed, only partially compensated); fix 4's dynamic centering fixed the OPACITY/BLUR "formed" state at 390 but not the ACTUAL VISIBILITY (the formed quote is centered behind the site's own nav at such a short frame height) — these are the CURRENT, ACTIVE problems R9 must solve.
   - **Ongoing/unresolved as of this summary**: I have identified the likely root causes and CSS-level fix directions for all three R9 issues (tesbandet: add `align-self:stretch` + `aspect-ratio:auto` overrides inside the mobile media query; Hōrai: likely increase the mobile case row height beyond `58svh` to push `ih` past the ~525-625px threshold, possibly combined with an anchor offset; Calyx: give step index 2's anchor an offset or switch to a `figcaption`-relative anchor so both photo and caption fit within the 450px frame) — but I have NOT yet re-read the current exact file state in this round to confirm line numbers, have NOT written the plan file, have NOT made any Edit calls, and have NOT begun any verification for R9. This is genuinely the very start of the round's work.

